1
00:04:25,384 --> 00:04:31,384
Welcome to the Jam!

2
00:08:50,769 --> 00:08:56,769
Space Jam: A New Legacy is a family, comedy,
adventure film directed by Malcolm D. Lee.

3
00:13:16,153 --> 00:13:22,153
When LeBron and his young son Dom are trapped in a digital space by a rogue A.I., LeBron must get them home safe by leading Bugs, Lola Bunny
and the whole gang of notoriously undisciplined Looney Tunes to victory over the A.I.'s digitized champions on the court.

4
00:17:41,538 --> 00:17:47,538
It's Tunes versus Goons in the highest-stakes challenge of his life.

5
00:22:06,923 --> 00:22:12,923
LeBron James, played by LeBron James.

6
00:26:32,307 --> 00:26:38,307
Al G. Rhythm, played by Don Cheadle.

7
00:30:57,692 --> 00:31:03,692
Dominic 'Dom' James, played by Cedric Joe.

8
00:35:23,076 --> 00:35:29,076
Bugs Bunny / Sylvester / Yosemite Sam / Fred
Flintstone (voice), played by Jeff Bergman.

9
00:39:48,461 --> 00:39:54,461
Speedy Gonzales (voice), played by Gabriel Iglesias.

10
00:44:13,846 --> 00:44:19,846
Lola Bunny (voice), played by Zendaya.

11
00:48:39,230 --> 00:48:45,230
Space Jam: A New Legacy is a 2021 American
live-action/animated sports comedy film, directed by Malcolm D.

12
00:53:04,615 --> 00:53:10,615
A sequel to Space Jam (1996), the film stars basketball player LeBron James as a fictionalized version of himself, in addition to featuring Don Cheadle,
Khris Davis and Sonequa Martin-Green in live-action roles, while Zendaya, Jeff Bergman and Eric Bauza headline the Looney Tunes voice cast.

13
00:57:29,999 --> 00:57:35,999
The film follows James enlisting the Looney Tunes' aid to win a basketball game in a Warner Bros.–themed virtual
world against its rogue artificial intelligence ruler after his youngest son is abducted by the AI.

14
01:01:55,384 --> 01:02:01,384
Discussions for a Space Jam sequel began following its release.

15
01:06:20,769 --> 01:06:26,769
Director Joe Pytka was attached to return, and Spike Brandt and Tony Cervone signed on as the animation
directors; however, the project stalled due to lead actor Michael Jordan's refusal to return.

16
01:10:46,153 --> 01:10:52,153
Several possible spin-offs focusing on other athletes, including Jeff Gordon,
Tiger Woods and Tony Hawk, were discussed but never materialized.

17
01:15:11,538 --> 01:15:17,538
After several years in development, a LeBron James-led sequel was announced in 2014 with
filming under director Terence Nance beginning in the Los Angeles area in June 2019.

18
01:19:36,923 --> 01:19:42,923
Nance left the project in July due to creative differences and was
replaced by Lee, with filming completed by September.

19
01:24:02,307 --> 01:24:08,307
Traditional animation was done by Company 3 and Tonic DNA, while visual effects
and computer animation were outsourced to Industrial Light & Magic.

20
01:28:27,692 --> 01:28:33,692
Space Jam: A New Legacy premiered in Los Angeles on July 12, 2021, and was
released nationwide in the United States by Warner Bros.

21
01:32:53,076 --> 01:32:59,076
Pictures on July 16, and through HBO Max for one month.

22
01:37:18,461 --> 01:37:24,461
The film was a commercial disappointment, grossing $164 million against a $150 million budget, and received generally negative
reviews from critics for its lack of humor, excessive runtime, and extensive product placement of WarnerMedia properties.

23
01:41:43,846 --> 01:41:49,846
It won three of its four Golden Raspberry Award
nominations, including Worst Actor for James.

24
01:46:09,230 --> 01:46:15,230
The film explores themes of sports, cartoon,
basketball, game, live action and animation.

25
01:50:34,615 --> 01:50:40,615
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
